.Dd September 21, 2026
.Dt ACPIPCC 4D
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm acpipcc
.Nd ACPI Platform Communications Channel
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/acpipcc.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
module is a kernel misc module implementing the Platform Communications
Channel (PCC) described in chapter 14 of the ACPI 6.6 specification.
.Pp
At load, the module parses the Platform Communications Channel Table
(PCCT), validating each subspace description.
If the firmware fails to
meet specification requirements during parsing the module fails all
subspace initialization.
When basic parsing of the firmware table fails
we assume that the firmware cannot be trusted.
.Pp
Initialisation then proceeds to map resources and install interrupt handlers.
If any error occurs in this phase of initialization the affected subspaces
fail to initialize.
.Pp
Finally, initialization publishes each usable subspace as a channel handle
that clients can retrieve based on subspace ID.
.Pp
Consumers obtain a channel with
.Xr pcc_chan_get 9F
and perform transactions serialised by the channel mutex.
.Ss Requirements on PCC consumers
PCC consumers must include the header file
.In sys/acpipcc.h .
.Pp
PCC consumers must also specify a link dependency on
.Dq misc/acpipcc .
(See the
.Fl N
option in
.Xr ld 1 ) .
.Pp
Channel handles are opaque.
Consumers must not attempt to inspect the handle
contents.
.Sh USAGE
A typical write transaction:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pcc_chan_t *pc = pcc_chan_get(subspace);
if (pc == NULL)
	return (DDI_FAILURE);

pcc_chan_lock(pc);
if (pcc_chan_write32(pc, REG_OFFSET, val) != DDI_SUCCESS ||
    pcc_chan_send(pc, CMD_WRITE, sizeof (val)) != DDI_SUCCESS) {
	pcc_chan_unlock(pc);
	pcc_chan_put(pc);
	return (DDI_FAILURE);
}
pcc_chan_unlock(pc);
pcc_chan_put(pc);
.Ed
.Pp
A read transaction sends a read command first and then collects the
results with the
.Xr pcc_chan_read32 9F
functions before unlocking.
The lock is always acquired before any payload access and released
after the results have been read; the accessors assert that it is
held.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa /kernel/misc/aarch64/acpipcc
64-bit aarch64 ELF kernel misc module
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pcc_chan 9F
.Rs
.%T ACPI Specification
.%U https://uefi.org/specifications
.Re
.Sh NOTES
This module is only available on aarch64 systems with ACPI firmware that
provides a Platform Communications Channel Table.
.Pp
Only channel types 1, 2 and 3 are presently supported.
Type 0 requires ACPI
hardware, type 4 is notification-only and has no current consumer and type 5
has no current consumer.
.Pp
The specification-deprecated notification functionality for types 1 and 2 is
not implemented.
